{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794382916170,"sessionID":"ses_e367638caffewcXcusTiMoC75h","part":{"id":"prt_1c98e6a2e001n7mTMt3LfMeHJI","messageID":"msg_1c98e58480018QdG7JPD3ru8kI","sessionID":"ses_e367638caffewcXcusTiMoC75h","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1794382916170,"sessionID":"ses_e367638caffewcXcusTiMoC75h","part":{"id":"prt_1c98e6a31001p60NpPOKyHrFGc","messageID":"msg_1c98e58480018QdG7JPD3ru8kI","sessionID":"ses_e367638caffewcXcusTiMoC75h","type":"text","text":"I need to check the `require_user()` return type: it returns a `sqlite3.Row` on success or a Flask response tuple on error. Using `isinstance(user, sqlite3.Row)` is a bit fragile but works. Let me refactor to a cleaner decorator-free approach with explicit checks — actually it works fine. Let me verify the app runs locally with a quick smoke test.","time":{"start":1794382916146,"end":1794382916165}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794382916353,"sessionID":"ses_e367638caffewcXcusTiMoC75h","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-a8c5728e8e6b0e2d","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"python3 -c \"import flask, werkzeug; print(flask.__version__, werkzeug.__version__)\" 2>&1 || echo \"flask not installed locally\"","workdir":"/workspace"},"output":"Traceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"<string>\", line 1, in <module>\n    import flask, werkzeug; print(flask.__version__, werkzeug.__version__)\n    ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\nModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'flask'\nflask not installed locally\n","metadata":{"output":"Traceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"<string>\", line 1, in <module>\n    import flask, werkzeug; print(flask.__version__, werkzeug.__version__)\n    ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\nModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'flask'\nflask not installed locally\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"python3 -c \"import flask, werkzeug; print(flask.__version__, werkzeug.__version__)\" 2>&1 || echo \"flask not installed locally\"","time":{"start":1794382916157,"end":1794382916283}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[]}},"id":"prt_1c98e6a35001g6VcNeTN82ngcy","sessionID":"ses_e367638caffewcXcusTiMoC75h","messageID":"msg_1c98e58480018QdG7JPD3ru8kI"}}
